    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1022-a2">

                <pb facs="1380" n="1256" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg1256"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cook</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Venezuelan Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Itriago Chacín</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 222</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your
                    Excellency that my Government has returned to me the Instrument of Ratification
                    by Venezuela of the Extradition Treaty between the United States and Venezuela
                    and additional Article thereto, with instructions to <pb facs="1381" n="1257"
                        xml:id="pg1257"/> obtain in substitution therefor, an Instrument of
                    Ratification by Venezuela incorporating the English as well as the Spanish
                    text.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>The original Extradition Treaty and additional article thereto which was signed
                    by the representatives of Venezuela and the United States, respectively, was in
                    both the Spanish and English languages, therefore the Instrument of Ratification
                    which you present my Government should include both texts. Otherwise, the
                    ratification would not be complete, as the English text is equally a part of the
                    Treaty with the Spanish.</p>
                <p>I therefore have the honor to request Your Excellency to be so kind as to furnish
                    me with an Instrument of Ratification in substitution of the one which has
                    already been returned to your Ministry, in which there is incorporated the
                    English as well as the Spanish text.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Willis C. Cook</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
